      "extract": "\\label{intro} Symbiotic stars (SySs) are usually interacting binaries, composed of a cool star, a hot component and a nebula. The cool component is a red giant which is a first giant branch (FGB) or an asymptotic giant branch (AGB) star. The hot component is a white dwarf (WD), a subdwarf, an accreting low-mass main-sequence star, or a neutron star \\citep{kw84,mur91}. The peculiar optical spectrum of SySs is a very",
      "extractCut": true
    },
