      "extract": "\\cite{v92} explained super-soft X-ray emissions by steady nuclear burning of hydrogen accreted onto WD. Most of the known SySs are sufficiently bright X-ray sources. As mentioned in Introduction, \\cite{mur97} divided X-ray sources into SSSs, SSs and relatively hard X-ray resources. It is well known that the SSSs in SySs are hot WDs whose photospheres can produce sufficiently hard ($h\\nu\\approx0.2$kev) photons. For",
